From 6a98ee33f6f3dc3d095f7eb2c42bc3fe00079337 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Covington <joshuacov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] char: raspberrypi-gpiomem: fix use-after-free on remove

rpi_gpiomem_remove() frees its private data and then reads priv->name
for its final log message. The freed memory may already have been
reused, and unbinding the driver oopses:

  pc : string+0x50/0x140
  lr : vsnprintf+0x1bc/0x64c
  Call trace:
   string+0x50/0x140 (P)
   vsnprintf+0x1bc/0x64c
   ...
   _dev_info+0x54/0x60
   rpi_gpiomem_remove+0x5c/0x6c
   platform_remove+0x20/0x30

Log the message before freeing the data, and terminate it with a
newline.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Covington <joshuacov@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/char/raspberrypi-gpiomem.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/char/raspberrypi-gpiomem.c
+++ b/drivers/char/raspberrypi-gpiomem.c
@@ -240,9 +240,8 @@ static void rpi_gpiomem_remove(struct pl
 	class_destroy(priv->class);
 	cdev_del(&priv->rpi_gpiomem_cdev);
 	unregister_chrdev_region(priv->devid, 1);
+	dev_info(dev, "%s driver removed - OK\n", priv->name);
 	kfree(priv);
-
-	dev_info(dev, "%s driver removed - OK", priv->name);
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id rpi_gpiomem_of_match[] = {
